note over DW,Trust #violet: 0. Load ETDA Trusted List (when a transaction needs it)
note right of DW #wheat:[CONDITION] before this flow (setup , outside the system) : the issuing agency is registered in iss.txt (DID , keys , credential types)\nand DW Core in wp.txt as wallet provider (certificate for WUA signatures , location of the WUA status lists) | WUA = WIA and key attestation\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0 9.9 (MUST) , 10.4.2
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] steps in the ETDA Trusted List Load sequence (first tab) | DW Core loads iss.txt (section 7) , VCVP Core loads wp.txt (section 8)
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Trusted List not usable (TRUST_LIST_EXPIRED / TRUST_LIST_UNAVAILABLE) : the calling step answers 503 Service Unavailable + Retry-After: 300\nnot the trust failure reason of that step , as in the ETDA Trusted List Load sequence

note over DW,Engine #orange: 7. DW Core Resolves the Credential Offer (inside request 1.2)

note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 13.4 (MUST NOT)  sensitive data only through a fully trusted server part of the wallet\n• 13.5 (MUST)  the Wallet validates the Credential Issuer\n• 13.10 (MUST)  a stored Bearer access token is kept secure
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core is the fully trusted server part of the wallet , it holds the pre-authorized_code and the access token (stored encrypted , not logged , not sent to the app)\nand makes every protocol call , the app signs and checks , the issuer trust check stays on the app
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] URLs from an offer or a QR are called only over https and never to internal addresses

DW->DW: Parse OfferUrl to get credential_offer_uri

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Protocol endpoints (/ssi , /.well-known) carry no Consumer-Key\noffer , token , credential , notification write VCVPAuditLog (Actor Channel = WALLET , no caller OrgCode)\nissuer metadata , authorization server metadata , nonce , DID document , vct type metadata are public reads\nalso written to VCVPAuditLog (no Actor)

DW->Core: Read offer from credential_offer_uri | GET /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/offer/{credentialId} (VCVP Core 11)\n(URL = credential_offer_uri in OfferUrl , {credentialSchemaId} and {credentialId} are engine ids inside it)
Core->Engine: Read offer from credential_offer_uri | GET /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/offer/{credentialId}
Engine-->Core: credential_issuer , credential_configuration_ids , grants.pre-authorized_code , grants.tx_code (when required)
Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Keep the engine interaction id (its value is the pre-authorized_code) in Credentials.InteractionId\nused only to find the credential from the access token later (sections 8.3 , 9 , 9.3) | credential found by {credentialId} in the offer path = CredentialId
Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 11 : the wallet read the offer of this credential (EngineCalls , Correlation.CredentialId)
DW<--Core: credential offer | credential_issuer , credential_configuration_ids , grants.pre-authorized_code , grants.tx_code (when required)
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] kept from the offer : pre-authorized_code (token request in section 8 , never sent to the app) , credential_issuer (issuer metadata URL , proof aud , trust check)\ncredential_configuration_ids (credential type) , grants.tx_code (input_mode , length , description) when present\nissuer metadata URL = /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer + path of credential_issuer
DW->DW: Keep the offer values and build the issuer metadata URL

DW->Core: Read issuer metadata from credential_issuer | GET /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId} (VCVP Core 12)\n(URL = /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer + path of credential_issuer from the offer , {protocolId} = OPENID4VCI_FINAL1 , {identifierId} = engine id of the issuer identifier , {credentialSchemaId})
Core->Engine: Read issuer metadata from credential_issuer |\nGET /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId}
Engine-->Core: credential_endpoint , nonce_endpoint , notification_endpoint , credential_configurations_supported
DW<--Core: issuer metadata | credential_endpoint , nonce_endpoint , notification_endpoint , credential_configurations_supported , credential_request_encryption , credential_response_encryption

DW->Core: Get authorization server metadata from authorization server | GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId} (VCVP Core 13)\n(URL = /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server + path of credential_issuer , the metadata declares no authorization_servers)
Core->Engine: Get authorization server metadata from authorization server |\nGET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId}
Engine-->Core: token_endpoint\ngrant_types_supported = [ pre-authorized_code , refresh_token ]
DW<--Core: authorization server metadata | token_endpoint
DW->DW: Keep token_endpoint , credential_endpoint , nonce_endpoint , notification_endpoint (for sections 8 and 9)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 12.2.4 (MUST , MUST NOT)  credential_issuer in metadata equals the identifier of the metadata URL\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.1 D.1.3 (MUST)  the offered configuration is in credential_configurations_supported
DW->DW: Check credential_issuer in metadata = credential_issuer from offer (simple string comparison)\nCheck credential_configuration_ids from the offer are in credential_configurations_supported
alt credential_issuer does not match / credential configuration not supported
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED (reason = ISSUER_METADATA_INVALID)\n(no nonce is requested , VC not issued , credential not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_METADATA_INVALID
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , the offer expires by itself
else Metadata valid
    DW->DW: Continue
end
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.4.3 (MUST)  TC-3 first round , the wallet checks the issuer\n• 9.10 (MUST)  reject at once when the local Trusted List check fails\n• appendix 8.1 D.1.4 (MUST)  check the issuer before authentication , stop at once on failure\n• 9.8 (MUST)  identity , key , status , validity period and scope checked by role\nOpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 13.5 (MUST)  the Wallet validates the Credential Issuer
note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : D.1.4 says the wallet checks the issuer with the Trusted List "on the device"\nquestion : may DW Core (the server part of the wallet) check instead of the app
note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : no field yet for the credential_issuer URL , issuer scope and status (12.1.4) , D.1.4 (MUST) rejects when the scope is unknown\nquestion : which fields will list them
DW->DW: Look up the issuer of credential_issuer in the cached Issuer Trusted List (iss.txt , ETDA Trusted List Load)\nservice type = issuer (ServiceTypeIdentifier) , organisation and service status = active , validity period current , credential type in the issuer scope
alt Issuer not in the Trusted List / not active / credential type not in scope
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED (reason = ISSUER_NOT_TRUSTED)\n(no nonce is requested , VC not issued , credential not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_NOT_TRUSTED
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , the offer expires by itself
else Issuer trusted
    DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Keep the issuer check in the issuance request (result = TRUSTED , checkedAt , Trusted List version)
end
note right of Engine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] c_nonce is valid 300 seconds and is not bound to the offer\nthe pre-authorized_code is valid 300 seconds (preAuthorizedCodeExpiresInSeconds)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 7 (MUST)  nonce endpoint\n• 13.8  a nonce is used until it is rejected
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] one nonce for every proof of the same request
DW->Core: Request nonce | POST nonce_endpoint (from issuer metadata) = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/nonce (VCVP Core 15)
Core->Engine: Request nonce | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/nonce
Engine-->Core: c_nonce
DW<--Core: c_nonce
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Keep in the issuance request : pre-authorized_code , c_nonce , OfferExpiresAt , endpoints (stored encrypted , not logged)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 12.2.4  credential_metadata , vct type metadata is preferred for display
note right of DW #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] the engine type metadata uses key instead of technicalKey and lang instead of locale , so the preview uses credential_metadata
DW->DW: Prepare the preview data : issuer name from the Issuer Trusted List , credential display and claims display (path , display name , mandatory)\nfrom credential_configurations_supported.{id}.credential_metadata , proof types and signing alg
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] response of 1.2 : issuanceSessionId , credential_issuer , c_nonce , preview data (issuer name , credential display , claims display , proof types , signing alg)\nissuerCheck (result = TRUSTED , checkedAt , Trusted List version = sequence / ETag of iss.txt) from the DW Core check in section 7\ntx_code requirement when the offer has one (input_mode , length , description , no code value)\nno pre-authorized_code and no Trusted List , DW Core made the checks
Mini<--DW: 200 (response of 1.2) | issuanceSessionId , c_nonce , preview data , issuerCheck , tx_code requirement
Mini->Mini: Keep proof types and signing alg (for proof JWT in section 8.1) , preview data (for 7.2) , c_nonce (for section 8)

note over User,Mini #lightblue: 7.2 User Reviews Credential
note right of Mini #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• chapter 14 SC-08 (informative)  names on the consent screen come from the Trusted List
note right of Mini #wheat:[STANDARD] EUDI ARF annex 2.02\n• ISSU_11 (SHALL)  the wallet tells the user who the issuer is before storing
note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] preview : issuer name from the Issuer Trusted List , credential type (credential display from metadata)\nlist of data in the credential (claims display names from metadata , no values) , issuer status from issuerCheck (trusted by ETDA , checked at)
Mini-->User: Show preview

alt Holder accepts credential
    User->Mini: Accept
    opt Offer requires tx_code (credential type with RequiredLoA IAL2.1 or higher)
        note right of Mini #wheat:[CONDITION] only for credential types with RequiredLoA IAL2.1 or higher (schema with transactionCode NUMERIC , 6 digits) , IAL1 types skip the tx_code steps
        note right of Mini #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 4.1.1 (RECOMMENDED)  show the tx_code description next to the input
        Mini-->User: Ask for the code sent by DW Core (second channel)\nlength and description from tx_code
        User->Mini: Enter tx_code
    end

    note over CoreApp,HSM #orange: 8. Issue Credential

    Mini->CoreApp: Sign the proofs for the token request (c_nonce from response of 1.2 , credential_issuer)
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] Client Attestation PoP : aud = credential_issuer
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Sign the Client Attestation PoP with the instance key
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Sign the wallet attestation request proof (new WIA) with the instance key
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• Appendix F.1 (MUST)  the key attestation nonce is the c_nonce
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] a key attestation is requested for every credential request
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] key attestation request proof : nonce = c_nonce (from response of 1.2)
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Sign the key attestation request proof with the holder key
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[CONDITION] only for credential types with RequiredLoA IAL2.3 or higher (schema RequireDpop = true)
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] the DPoP key is created in the TEE once , DPoP proof : htm POST , htu = token endpoint , jti , iat
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Sign a DPoP proof with the DPoP key
    CoreApp-->Mini: Client Attestation PoP + wallet attestation request proof + key attestation request proof + DPoP proof (when required)
    Mini->DW: Request a new WIA , the key attestation and the access token + Token | POST /dw/v1/issuance/token (DW endpoint 05)\n(issuanceSessionId , wallet attestation request proof , Client Attestation PoP , key attestation request proof , DPoP proof when required , tx_code when required)
    DW->DW: Check OfferExpiresAt , when it has passed renew the offer first (same steps as the expired branch below)
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 10.5.1 (SHOULD)  WUA once-only or in a batch\n• 10.5.2 (MUST)  client_status and key_storage_status use Token Status Lists of the wallet provider\nOpenID4VCI 1.0\n• Appendix F.1 (MUST)  key attestation nonce = c_nonce
    DW->DW: As the wallet provider : verify the request proofs (instance key for the WIA , registered holder key and c_nonce for the key attestation) , wallet unit status = ACTIVE
    alt Wallet unit not active / request proof invalid
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED (reason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED)\n(VC not issued , credential not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of /dw/v1/issuance/token) | reason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED
        Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , the offer expires by itself
    else Wallet unit active
        note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• Appendix D.1 (MUST)  exp present in the key attestation with the jwt proof type\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 10.5.1 (SHOULD)  short-lived WUA\n• 10.4.2  the Wallet Provider Trusted List carries the certificate that verifies WUA signatures\n• 9.2  no CA certificate is needed , trust comes from the listing in the Trusted List\nEUDI TS3 v1.5.2\n• 2.2.1.2 (SHALL)  the WIA is signed with the key of the certificate in x5c , the certificate validates against the Wallet Provider Trusted List
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] both signed with the one wallet provider key of DW , header x5c = wallet provider certificate (no iss)\nWIA : valid 300 seconds | cnf , wallet_name , wallet_version , wallet_solution_certification_information , wallet_link , client_status { status , exp }\nKA : exp = iat + 300 seconds (the same as c_nonce , bound to the c_nonce of one request) | nonce = c_nonce , attested_keys = holder public key , key_storage , certification , key_storage_status { status , exp }
        DW->DW: Issue a new WIA and a key attestation for this request
    end
    note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] token request from DW Core\ntoken_endpoint from authorization server metadata\nheaders : OAuth-Client-Attestation = the new WIA , OAuth-Client-Attestation-PoP , DPoP (when required)\nbody : pre-authorized_code + tx_code (when the offer requires it)
    DW->Core: Request access token with pre-authorized_code (from offer) | POST token_endpoint = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/token (VCVP Core 14)
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.1 D.1.9 (MUST)  check the Wallet Attestation before an access token (TC-2)\n• 12.8 (MUST)  fetch the list when the connection needs the trust decision\n• 10.4.2  the Wallet Provider Trusted List carries the certificate that verifies WUA signatures\nOpenID4VCI 1.0\n• Appendix E (MUST)  the Wallet Attestation is signed by an issuer the Credential Issuer trusts\nEUDI TS3 v1.5.2\n• 2.2.1.2 (SHALL)  WIA signature under the x5c certificate , the certificate validates against the Wallet Provider Trusted List
note right of Core #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : wp.txt has no field yet for the certificate that signs the WUA (10.4.2)\nquestion : which field holds it
Core->Core: Check the x5c signing certificate of the WIA against the cached Wallet Provider Trusted List (wp.txt , ETDA Trusted List Load)\nrole (service type = wallet provider , ServiceTypeIdentifier) , certificate , organisation and service status = active , validity period current
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.6 (MUST)  replay protection (nonce , jti)
note right of Core #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] the engine accepts the same WIA-PoP jti on a second offer
note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core keeps the used WIA-PoP jti because the engine accepts the same jti\nremove the jti check and Credentials.WiaPopJti when the engine rejects a WIA-PoP with a used jti
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] where : VCVP Core looks the jti up in its own Credentials table (WiaPopJti , unique index)\nwhen recorded : only after the engine issues the access token (branch Access token issued below) , a rejected request does not record it
Core->Core: Check the WIA-PoP jti is not recorded as used (Credentials.WiaPopJti , unique index)
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 10.5.2 (MUST)  WIA revocation uses the Token Status List of the wallet provider (client_status)\n• appendix 8.1 D.1.9 (MUST)  wallet instance status checked before an access token
note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core checks client_status because the engine does not for these schemas (the WIA of a revoked wallet unit gets a token)\nremove this step when the engine checks client_status
note right of Core #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : wp.txt has no field yet for where the WUA status list is published (10.4.2)\nquestion : which field holds it
Core->DW: Get the WIA status list | GET client_status.status_list.uri (DW endpoint 16 , Token Status List of DW Core)
DW-->Core: Status List JWT (statuslist+jwt)
Core->Core: Check the WIA status at idx = 0x00 VALID\nsignature with the wallet provider key , typ , sub , exp , cached up to ttl and at most 1 hour
    alt Wallet provider not in the Trusted List / not active / WIA-PoP jti used before / WIA revoked
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 14 (FailureReason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED , Correlation.CredentialId)
        DW<--Core: 401 invalid_client
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , credential not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of /dw/v1/issuance/token) | reason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED
        Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , the offer expires by itself
    else Wallet provider trusted
        Core->Core: Continue
    end
    note right of Core #wheat:[CONDITION] DPoP is used only for credential types with RequiredLoA IAL2.3 or higher (schema RequireDpop = true) , lower types use Bearer
    note right of Core #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : D.2 says "consider" DPoP at IAL2.3 , D.3 (MUST) requires it\nquestion : is DPoP required from IAL2.3 (follow D.3)
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• appendix 8.1 D.3 (MUST)  DPoP jti not used again , from IAL2.3\n• appendix 8.1 D.1.6 (proposal)  random jti per request\nRFC 9449\n• 11.1  a used jti is declined in the accepted time window , keep only a hash
    note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core keeps the DPoP proof jti because the engine accepts a used jti\nremove this check and DpopProofJtis table when the engine declines a used DPoP jti
    note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] VCVP Core checks that DPoP is present because the engine has no setting to require it (a token request without DPoP gets Bearer)\nremove this check when the engine can require DPoP per schema
    Core->Core: Check the request has a DPoP header , when CredentialSchemas.RequireDpop = true
    note right of Core #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] the engine accepts a DPoP proof while iat is within 5 minutes , plus 1 minute leeway (fixed in the engine code)
    Core->Core: Look up the DPoP proof in DpopProofJtis table (JtiHash , Htu) , when the request has a DPoP header
    alt DPoP required but missing / DPoP jti used before
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 14 (FailureReason = DPOP_REQUIRED / DPOP_PROOF_REUSED , Correlation.CredentialId)
        DW<--Core: 400 invalid_dpop_proof
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , credential not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of /dw/v1/issuance/token) | reason = FailureReason
        Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    else DPoP valid or not required
        note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] DpopProofJtis table\nJtiHash = hash of jti , Htu = htu of the proof\nExpiresAt = now + 360 seconds , deleted by the database when expired
        Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store the DPoP proof in DpopProofJtis table , when the request has a DPoP header
        Core->Core: Continue
    end
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 13.10 (MUST)  no long-lived access token unless sender-constrained\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.6 (SHOULD)  short-lived access token
    note right of Engine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] the access token is valid 300 seconds (tokenExpiresInSeconds) , Bearer or DPoP-bound when a DPoP proof is sent , no refresh_token is returned
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 10.5.1 (SHOULD)  short-lived WUA , revocation is the backup\ndraft-ietf-oauth-attestation-based-client-auth-12\n• 7.1 (MUST)  the client attestation is fresh per local policy
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] WIA freshness policy = exp checked by the engine , DW Core sets exp = iat + 300 seconds , VCVP Core makes no extra iat check
    Core->Engine: Request access token with pre-authorized_code (from offer) | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/token\npre-authorized code + tx_code (when required) + OAuth-Client-Attestation , OAuth-Client-Attestation-PoP
    Engine->Engine: Check both headers are present (OAuth-Client-Attestation , OAuth-Client-Attestation-PoP) , every schema sets requiresWalletInstanceAttestation
    Engine->Engine: Verify the WIA signature , the PoP signature and the PoP audience
    Engine->Engine: Check the WIA exp has not passed (60 seconds leeway)

    alt tx_code wrong (offer requires tx_code)
        note right of Engine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] after one wrong code the right code is refused (400 credential_request_denied)\nthe credential state is ERROR and share is refused (400 BR_0002) , a new credential and offer with a new code are needed\na request without the code gets 400 invalid_request and the right code still works after it
        Engine-->Core: 400 invalid_grant
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 14 (FailureReason = TX_CODE_INVALID , Correlation.CredentialId)
        DW<--Core: 400 | FailureReason = TX_CODE_INVALID
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED (reason = TX_CODE_INVALID)\n(VC not issued , credential not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of /dw/v1/issuance/token) | reason = TX_CODE_INVALID
        Mini-->User: Show error : the code is not correct , request the credential again to get a new code
    else WIA expired (exp passed)
        Engine-->Core: error (WIA expired)
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 14 (FailureReason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED , Correlation.CredentialId)
        DW<--Core: 401 invalid_client
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , credential not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of /dw/v1/issuance/token) | reason = WALLET_ATTESTATION_FAILED
        Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    else Pre-authorized code expired / invalid
        Engine-->Core: error
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 14 (FailureReason = PRE_AUTHORIZED_CODE_INVALID , Correlation.CredentialId)
        DW<--Core: 400 | error = invalid_grant , FailureReason = PRE_AUTHORIZED_CODE_INVALID (offer expired)
        note right of DW #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] c_nonce and the PoP audience (credential_issuer) are not bound to the offer , so the same request continues with a renewed offer
        note right of DW #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] c_nonce is valid 300 seconds , the c_nonce from response of 1.2 has expired\nthe key attestation needs a new c_nonce , so the app signs the section 8 proofs again
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = OFFER_EXPIRED (the offer is renewed at the next request)
        alt Offer has tx_code
            Mini<--DW: 409 (response of /dw/v1/issuance/token) | reason = OFFER_EXPIRED
            Mini-->User: Show "The code has expired" with the button "Send a new code"
            User->Mini: Tap "Send a new code"
            Mini->DW: Request a new code | POST /dw/v1/issuance/tx-code (DW endpoint 18)\n(issuanceSessionId)
        else Offer without tx_code
            DW->Core: Request a new c_nonce | POST nonce_endpoint (VCVP Core 15)
            DW<--Core: c_nonce
            Mini<--DW: 409 (response of /dw/v1/issuance/token) | reason = OFFER_EXPIRED , new c_nonce
            note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] new Client Attestation PoP , key attestation request proof , DPoP proof when required
            Mini->Mini: Repeat section 8 with the new c_nonce , it calls /dw/v1/issuance/token (DW endpoint 05) again
