        DW<--Core: DID document
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] URL = vct in the credential , {orgId} = engine id of the issuer organisation
        DW->Core: Get credential type description (vct type metadata) | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{credentialSchemaId}/SD_JWT_VC (VCVP Core 18)
        Core->Engine: Get credential type description (vct type metadata) | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{credentialSchemaId}/SD_JWT_VC
        Engine-->Core: credential type description (vct type metadata)
        DW<--Core: credential type description (vct type metadata)
        note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : 12.6 (MUST) checks the validity period of each issuer key , the Trusted List has no per-key period\nquestion : will the Trusted List list each issuer key with its start and end date
        note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] RFC 9901 (SD-JWT)\n• 7.1 , 7.2 (MUST)  verify the issuer signature and every disclosure\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 12.6 (MUST NOT)  no DID document key instead of the Trusted List key
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] the DID before # in kid = iss , the key with id = kid is in the issuer DID document under assertionMethod and listed for the issuer in the Trusted List\nthen an SD-JWT library checks the signature and every disclosure , alg matches the key type (ES256 = EC P-256 , EdDSA = Ed25519) , not taken from the header alone (11.3 MUST)\nthe key comes from kid (8.4.3 step 4) and must be listed in the Trusted List (12.6) , not from JWKS (D.1.11 [28])
        DW->DW: Verify issuer signature (Check 2)
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Check 3 : nbf <= now , exp > now when present
        DW->DW: Check the validity window (Check 3)
        note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Token Status List draft-21\n• 8.3 (MUST , MUST NOT)  check the token before its status , no status fetch for an invalid token\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 13.3 (MUST NOT)  no status check when the token check fails
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] status list request : Accept: application/statuslist+jwt
        DW->Core: Get the status list | GET status.status_list.uri = /ssi/revocation/v1/list/{id} (VCVP Core 31)
        Core->Engine: Get the status list | GET /ssi/revocation/v1/list/{id}
        Engine-->Core: Status List JWT (typ statuslist+jwt)
        DW<--Core: Status List JWT
        note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] Token Status List draft-21\n• 5.1 (MUST , REQUIRED , RECOMMENDED)  typ , sub , iat , exp , ttl\n• 8.3 (MUST)  check exp when present , reject idx out of range\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.4.4 (MUST)  fail closed
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] accept only 0x00 (VALID) at idx , cache by ttl
        note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for ETDA | Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\nissue : 13.2 says the profile fixes one Token Status List revision (draft-18 and draft-21 differ)\nquestion : which revision
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Check 4 : signature by the issuer key (alg matches the key type , 11.3 MUST) , sub = status_list.uri , iat , exp when present , value at idx = 0x00 (VALID)
        DW->DW: Check the status (Check 4)
        note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] SD-JWT VC draft-19\n• 6 (MUST)  verify a retrieved document against its #integrity value
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Check 5 : hash of the credential type description downloaded from VCVP Core 18 = vct#integrity in the credential
        DW->DW: Check the credential type description (Check 5)

        alt Any check fails (Check 1 to 5)
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Failure reason per check (for developers)\nCheck 1 issuer not in the Trusted List , not active or type not in scope : ISSUER_NOT_TRUSTED\nCheck 2 issuer signature invalid or key not listed in the Trusted List : VERIFICATION_FAILED\nCheck 3 outside the validity window : CREDENTIAL_NOT_VALID\nCheck 4 status not VALID or status list invalid : CREDENTIAL_STATUS_INVALID\nCheck 5 the credential type description does not match vct#integrity : CREDENTIAL_TYPE_MISMATCH\nDW Core sends the reason to VCVP Core in event_description of the notification (OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 11.1 , OPTIONAL)\nVCVP Core reads event_description before forwarding and stores it in FailureReason , the engine does not keep it
            DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , credential not added)
            note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 11 (MUST)  the notification carries a valid access token
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core sends the notification right away (after the failed check) , the access token is valid 300 seconds
            note right of Engine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] after the access token expires the engine answers 400 invalid_token and the credential state does not change (tested on engine v1.88.1)
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core holds the access token (section 8)
            note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 11.1  credential_failure for failures not caused by the user , credential_deleted only when the user caused it
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] notification_endpoint from issuer metadata , kept by DW
            DW->Core: Notify credential_failure with notification_id + access token | POST notification_endpoint = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (VCVP Core 19)
            note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] RFC 9449\n• 7.1 (MUST)  a DPoP-bound access token is sent with the DPoP scheme and a DPoP proof
            note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] the engine accepts a used DPoP jti at the notification endpoint too (tested on engine v1.88.1)\nremove this check when the engine declines a used DPoP jti
            Core->Core: Check the DPoP proof jti in DpopProofJtis table as in VCVP Core 16 , when the request has a DPoP header\n(used before : [ERROR AUDIT] FailureReason = DPOP_PROOF_REUSED , 400 invalid_dpop_proof | not used : store it)
            Core->Engine: Notify credential_failure with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification
            Engine->Engine: State ACCEPTED → ERROR
            Engine-->Core: 204
            note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] Credentials table\nStatus = ISSUANCE_FAILED\nWalletNotification : Event = credential_failure , ReceivedAt , FailureReason from event_description\ncredential found by the access token of the notification request = InteractionId
            Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Update Credentials table : Status = ISSUANCE_FAILED , WalletNotification
            Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 19 (FailureReason = reason from event_description , event = credential_failure , Correlation.CredentialId)
            DW<--Core: 204
            Mini<--DW: Error (response of /dw/v1/issuance/credential) | reason of the failed check
            Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
            note over User,Mini #wheat: VC not stored , credential not added
        else Verification passed
            Mini<--DW: 200 (response of /dw/v1/issuance/credential) | credential (SD_JWT_VC + all disclosures)

            note over CoreApp #lightblue: 9.1 Credential Storage Model (on device or cloud)
            note right of CoreApp #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for the Mobile App (Core ทางรัฐ) team\nissue : two storage modes are kept in the design\nquestion : which mode stays
            Mini->CoreApp: Store the credential (SD_JWT_VC + all disclosures)
            alt Storage mode = ON_DEVICE
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] ON_DEVICE : the app keeps the full token , can present offline , the backend keeps references only
                CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store the full token (SD_JWT_VC + disclosures) in the on-device database
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[DATA STORE] on-device database\ncredentialId , credentialType , vct\nissuer DID / issuer display name\nschemaId\nvalidFrom / validUntil\nstatus reference ( uri + idx )\ndisplay metadata
                CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store credential metadata in on-device database
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Bind credentialId to holder key reference\nBind credentialId to deviceId
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Mark credential as available for presentation

            else Storage mode = CLOUD (encrypted on the device before upload)
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] CLOUD : the token is encrypted on the device , DW keeps ciphertext and metadata , presenting needs a network connection
                note right of CoreApp #FFCDD2:[PENDING] waiting for the Mobile App (Core ทางรัฐ) team and the DW team\nissue : the data key cannot be recovered when the device is lost , metadata on DW is readable\nquestion : 1. recover the data key or issue again (suggested : issue again , cnf is bound to the old device key)\n2. which metadata fields stay readable (suggested : only what DW needs , for example status reference and expiry , the rest encrypted)
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] data key protected by secure hardware (Secure Enclave / Android Keystore)
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Encrypt the full token (SD_JWT_VC + disclosures) on the device
                CoreApp->DW: Store encrypted credential + Token | POST /dw/v1/credentials (DW endpoint 10)\n(credentialId , encrypted token , credential metadata)
                note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW cloud storage\nCitizenId , deviceId , credentialId\nencrypted token (DW cannot decrypt it)\ncredential metadata : credentialType , vct , issuer DID , validFrom / validUntil , status reference ( uri + idx )
                DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store encrypted credential in DW cloud storage
                CoreApp<--DW: 201 | cloud reference
                CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store credential metadata + cloud reference in on-device database
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Bind credentialId to holder key reference\nBind credentialId to deviceId
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Mark credential as available for presentation

            end

            note over CoreApp #lightblue: 9.2 Secure Local Storage and Access Policy
            note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] app security baseline (set once in the app , not per credential , both storage modes)\ntarget : OWASP MASVS-STORAGE level L2 (the library provides only L1 , the gap must be implemented)\nsecure local storage : Android EncryptedSharedPreferences / Room encrypted DB , iOS Keychain\nenvelope encryption : KEK in secure hardware protects DEK on disk , DEK encrypts the data files\nfile protection : unreadable while the screen is locked , not only until first unlock after boot\naccess : biometric / PIN / device unlock\npersonal data : no readable claim copies without justification\nholder private key : Secure Enclave / Android Keystore / StrongBox , not exportable\nusage policy : holder confirmation before presentation , holder signing before VP submission
CoreApp-->Mini: Credential stored | credentialId

            note over CoreApp,Engine #lightblue: 9.3 Wallet confirms receipt
            Mini->DW: Report issuance result + Token | POST /dw/v1/issuance/result (DW endpoint 08)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , result = ACCEPTED)
            DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ACCEPTED
            note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 11 (MUST)  valid access token at the Notification Endpoint\n• 13.4  DW Core is the server part of the wallet
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core sends the notification right away (when the app reports the result) , the access token is valid 300 seconds
            note right of Engine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] after the access token expires the engine answers 400 invalid_token and the credential state does not change (tested on engine v1.88.1)
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core sends the notification , the app sends only the result
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] notification_endpoint from issuer metadata , kept by DW
            DW->Core: Notify credential_accepted with notification_id + access token | POST notification_endpoint = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (VCVP Core 19)
            note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] RFC 9449\n• 7.1 (MUST)  a DPoP-bound access token is sent with the DPoP scheme and a DPoP proof
            note right of Core #B3E5FC:[WORKAROUND] the engine accepts a used DPoP jti at the notification endpoint too (tested on engine v1.88.1)\nremove this check when the engine declines a used DPoP jti
            Core->Core: Check the DPoP proof jti in DpopProofJtis table as in VCVP Core 16 , when the request has a DPoP header\n(used before : [ERROR AUDIT] FailureReason = DPOP_PROOF_REUSED , 400 invalid_dpop_proof | not used : store it)
            note right of Engine #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] the engine sets ACCEPTED when the credential is issued , not on notification\ncredential_accepted does not change state\ncredential_failure → ERROR | credential_deleted → REJECTED\nERROR and REJECTED set the Token Status List entry to INVALID , suspend , reactivate and revoke are refused afterwards (400 BR_0366)
            Core->Engine: Notify credential_accepted with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification
            Engine-->Core: 204 (state stays ACCEPTED)
            note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] Credentials table\nWalletNotification : Event = credential_accepted , ReceivedAt\ncredential found by the access token of the notification request = InteractionId
            Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store the wallet receipt in Credentials table (WalletNotification)
            Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 19 : the wallet confirmed it stored the credential (event = credential_accepted , Correlation.CredentialId)
            DW<--Core: 204
            Mini<--DW: 200 (response of /dw/v1/issuance/result) | result recorded

            Mini-->User: Show the credential with a VC badge (claims from the stored VC)
        end

    end

else Holder rejects credential
    User->Mini: Reject
    Mini->DW: Reject offer + Token | POST /dw/v1/issuance/reject (DW endpoint 09)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , reason = HOLDER_REJECTED)
    DW->Core: Reject credential | POST /api/credential/v1/offer-reject (VCVP Core 20)
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] caller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN , the credential belongs to the citizen of the request
    Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) and caller authorization
    alt Consumer-Key invalid or missing
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 20 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED , OrgCode and Actor empty)
        DW<--Core: 401 + WWW-Authenticate | FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED
        note over DW,Core #wheat: Reject not recorded in VCVP , the offer still expires by itself
    else Caller not authorized
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 20 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
        DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
        note over DW,Core #wheat: Reject not recorded in VCVP , the offer still expires by itself
    else Caller authorized

        note over Core #pink: 11. Handle Holder Reject
        note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] VCVP Core does not call the engine , the offer expires by itself
        Core->Core: Update status HOLDER_REJECTED
        note right of Core #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] proof that the holder declined the credential (VCVPAuditLog)\nEventType = CREDENTIAL_OFFER_REJECTED\nActor (Channel = WALLET)\nReasonDetail\nCorrelation.CredentialId\nEventTime\nIntegrity.Hash , Integrity.PrevHash
        Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 20 : the holder declined the credential (status = HOLDER_REJECTED , Correlation.CredentialId)

        DW<--Core: 200
    end
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = HOLDER_REJECTED
    Mini<--DW: Cancel issuance
    Mini-->User: Credential not issued , credential not added
end


@enduml
